{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeSum","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BranchIntegerPinning","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ConstantOffOnePoint","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.RestrictScalars"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelope_integrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.envelope_integrate","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly.lean#L126-L148","doc":"**From `S′ = 2φ` off one point to `S φ = S 0 + φ²`.**\n\n`constant_of_hasDerivWithinAt_zero_off_point` applied to `φ ↦ S φ − φ²`. The one\nexceptional point is `φ₀`, where the discriminant vanishes\n(`exists_unit_circle_disc_zero`) and no differentiable root labelling exists.\n\nAt `b = π` this is `S(π) − S(0) = π²`, which is what the transport wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchDiff_eq_zero_of_continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchDiff_eq_zero_of_continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly.lean#L111-L122","doc":"**The pinning, reduced to `hcont`.** Given that the branch difference is\ncontinuous on `[a,b]` and vanishes at `a`, and that its exponential is `1`\nthroughout — which the two lemmas above supply from Vieta — it vanishes\nidentically.\n\nThis is `eq_zero_of_continuousOn_of_exp_eq_one` with its algebraic input\ndischarged: **only continuity is left**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_logSumB_add_log_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_logSumB_add_log_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly.lean#L100-L109","doc":"`exp(Σⱼ log(1 − yⱼ/x) + log x) = 1`, from the other Vieta product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_logSumA_sub_log_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exp_logSumA_sub_log_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly.lean#L88-L98","doc":"`exp(Σⱼ log(1 − x·yⱼ) − log x) = 1`, from the Vieta product. This is the\n`hexp` hypothesis of `eq_zero_of_continuousOn_of_exp_eq_one`, discharged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_of_partial_y_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_of_partial_y_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeAssembly.lean#L65-L84","doc":"**The envelope theorem.** If the `y`-partial vanishes at the point, the total\nderivative along any differentiable path is the `x`-part alone — `y′` cancels.\n\nThis is the whole reason the envelope argument needs only *existence* of\n`dyⱼ/dx`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}